                        "sense_id": "e4316b5b-2a9d-37b1-8255-73db06444b41",
                        "entry_id": "8253d527-043b-3a72-ba6f-5507f97c7538",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Vague; ill-defined; unclear."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac1e8347-cc37-4391-9732-cbe5f61c67ab",
                                "sense_id": "e4316b5b-2a9d-37b1-8255-73db06444b41",
                                "text": "Yet such Commissions were awarded, and far more frequently than might be supposed in view of the infinitely wider gulf—both social and educational—which divided the eighteenth-century Officer from the rank and file, than the penumbrous border line which separates them today."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e90707d1-20a1-4d38-8c89-47a06798d70f",
                                "sense_id": "e4316b5b-2a9d-37b1-8255-73db06444b41",
                                "text": "Everyone knows God in his penumbrous knowledge of common esse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f0cb8f7-ad35-427b-87d8-115cb3b032a2",
                                "sense_id": "e4316b5b-2a9d-37b1-8255-73db06444b41",
                                "text": "This is that from which metaphor springs dissatisfying, penumbrous - the silence on occult matters, or those of predestination, of genetics or environment - and the source of circumlocution, the ambiguous alchemical directives."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d01591e-997e-4c50-a129-3ef9a3a566e5",
                                "sense_id": "e4316b5b-2a9d-37b1-8255-73db06444b41",
                                "text": "In the early nineteenth century, when high school and college education was a rare experience for the average American citizen, judicial determination of vague, penumbrous fundamental rights was carried out by the educated classes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
